{
  "description": "A corrected BERT4Rec cold start for sequential recommendation across Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, and CDs_and_Vinyl. Train one independent model per category using masked-target learning and appended-mask inference. Compare trials by macro-average validation HR@10 under the fixed RecHarness evaluator.",
  "motivation": "Establish a valid, reproducible BERT4Rec baseline so improvements reflect modeling changes rather than target leakage, padding errors, altered splits, or evaluator differences. The supplied description defines an experimental protocol, not a new algorithm or measured improvement.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four dataset routes, the supplied splits, and DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']. Use at most 200 epochs and exactly 200 batches per epoch. Histories are left-padded; readout must select the final nonpadding position. Reserve a mask token, hide supervised targets during bidirectional training, and append a mask for inference. Save artifacts beneath the trial directory and update the embedded predictor writer whenever architecture changes. Prediction must load exactly one trained checkpoint per category, without independent-model fusion. Preserve the ModelView compatibility interfaces and the required DiagnosisProbe and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt APIs. Diagnostics must use measured quantities and available public data. No validation results or concrete baseline architecture details were supplied.",
  "pseudocode": "Set preprocessing seed to 0 and training seed to 42.\nFor each of the four categories:\n    Load the supplied training and validation splits.\n    Initialize the supplied corrected BERT4Rec architecture.\n    For up to 200 epochs, with 200 batches per epoch:\n        Sample left-padded histories using the family-specific sampler.\n        Hide selected targets using the reserved mask token.\n        Optimize the masked-target recommendation objective.\n    Save one model checkpoint and matching architecture configuration.\nGenerate working/predict.py with consistent category routing and model loading.\nAt inference, reserve space for an appended mask, encode the history, and score candidate items from the final nonpadding mask representation.\nLet the host independently evaluate validation HR@10 and macro-average across categories.",
  "originality": {
    "score": 2,
    "positive": "Provides explicit corrections for leakage prevention, left-padding readout, and checkpoint–predictor consistency.",
    "negative": "Uses established BERT4Rec principles; no novel architecture, loss, or empirical finding is described."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Provides a controlled foundation for exploring masking strategies, optimization, and jointly trained architectural changes within BERT4Rec.",
    "negative": "Improvement remains unverified and must be demonstrated within the fixed validation protocol and shared GPU budget."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The supplied corrected baseline and fixed interfaces constrain implementation scope.",
    "negative": "Correct masking, left-padding handling, diagnostic compatibility, and matching training and inference architectures require careful implementation."
  }
}
